Simulated cross-origin call: adding Origin: http://localhost:3000 in Postman does not make
Postman enforce anything; it only makes the server produce the same CORS headers it would give a
browser, which lets you verify them. Origin: http://localhost:8080 (same as the API itself) is
treated as same-origin, so no CORS headers appear.
